11354:^DD(2,".121",21,1,0)="The Bad Address Indicator field applies to the address at which the patient"
11355:^DD(2,".121",21,2,0)="resides.  This field should be set as follows (if applicable):"
11356:^DD(2,".121",21,3,0)=" "
11357:^DD(2,".121",21,4,0)="    ""UNDELIVERABLE"" - Bad Address based on returned mail."
11358:^DD(2,".121",21,5,0)="    ""HOMELESS"" - Patient is known to be homeless."
11359:^DD(2,".121",21,6,0)="    ""OTHER"" - Other Bad Address Reason"
11360:^DD(2,".121",21,7,0)=" "
11361:^DD(2,".121",21,8,0)="Setting this field will prevent a Bad Address from being shared with HEC"
11362:^DD(2,".121",21,9,0)="and other VAMC facilities."
11363:^DD(2,".121",21,10,0)=" "
11364:^DD(2,".121",21,11,0)=" "
11365:^DD(2,".121",21,12,0)="Once the Bad Address Indicator is set, incoming ""newer"" addresses will"
11366:^DD(2,".121",21,13,0)="automatically remove the Bad Address Indicator, and allow the ""updated"""
11367:^DD(2,".121",21,14,0)="address to be transmitted to HEC and other VAMC facilities. To manually"
11368:^DD(2,".121",21,15,0)="remove the Bad Address Indicator enter the ""@"" symbol."
11369:^DD(2,".121",23,0)="^.001^9^9^3140707^^^^"
11370:^DD(2,".121",23,1,0)="This field is being used in conjunction with Patient Address fields"
11371:^DD(2,".121",23,2,0)=".111, .1112, .112, .113, .114, .115, .116, and .117, which are located"
11372:^DD(2,".121",23,3,0)="in the Patient (#2) file."
11373:^DD(2,".121",23,4,0)=""
11374:^DD(2,".121",23,5,0)="A programmer API, $$BADADR^DGUTL3(DFN) will allow the return of the Bad"
