16542:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",0)="^^8^8^2920429^"
16543:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",1,0)="When the eligibility code is changed, this cross-reference removes the"
16544:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",2,0)="data in the ELIGIBILITY STATUS field.  This only occurs if neither the"
16545:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",3,0)="original eligibility code nor the new eligibility code (the one being"
16546:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",4,0)="entered) is DOM. PATIENT.  If either is DOM. PATIENT, no update occurs."
16547:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",5,0)=" "
16548:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",6,0)="Since the DOM. PATIENT eligibility is being inactivated with MAS 5.2,"
16549:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",7,0)="the conditional on this cross-reference will be removed in a future "
16550:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"%D",8,0)="version of MAS."
16551:^DD(2,".361",1,3,"DT")=2920429
16552:^DD(2,".361",1,4,0)="2^AEL^MUMPS"
16553:^DD(2,".361",1,4,1)="S ^DPT(""AEL"",DA,+X)="""""
16554:^DD(2,".361",1,4,2)="K ^DPT(""AEL"",DA,+X)"
16555:^DD(2,".361",1,5,0)="2^AENR361^MUMPS"
16556:^DD(2,".361",1,5,1)="D AUTOUPD^DGENA2(DA)"
16557:^DD(2,".361",1,5,2)="D AUTOUPD^DGENA2(DA)"
16558:^DD(2,".361",1,5,3)="DO NOT DELETE"
16559:^DD(2,".361",1,5,"%D",0)="^^2^2^2970715^^"
16560:^DD(2,".361",1,5,"%D",1,0)="This cross-reference is used to update the patient's current Patient Enrollment "
16561:^DD(2,".361",1,5,"%D",2,0)="record."
16562:^DD(2,".361",1,5,"DT")=2970715
16563:^DD(2,".361",3)="Select from the available list the eligibility code which best defines this applicant's primary entitlement to care.  For more detailed information, enter ??."
16564:^DD(2,".361",12)="Applicable code based on veteran or non-veteran status."
16565:^DD(2,".361","12.1")="S DFN=DA D ECD^DGLOCK1"
16566:^DD(2,".361",20,0)="^.3LA^1^1"
16567:^DD(2,".361",20,1,0)="ECD"
16568:^DD(2,".361",21,0)="^.001^45^45^3060321^^^^"
16569:^DD(2,".361",21,1,0)="Select from the available listing the appropriate eligibility code for"
16570:^DD(2,".361",21,2,0)="this applicant.  For non-veteran applicants a wide variety of choices"
16571:^DD(2,".361",21,3,0)="are available.  For veteran applicants the choices are screened [in the"
16572:^DD(2,".361",21,4,0)="following order] dependent on the responses to other prompts:"
16573:^DD(2,".361",21,5,0)="   "
16574:^DD(2,".361",21,6,0)="1.  If the SERVICE CONNECTED prompt (field .301) is answered YES"
16575:^DD(2,".361",21,7,0)="    only the following two choices are available:"
16576:^DD(2,".361",21,8,0)="    "
16577:^DD(2,".361",21,9,0)="    a.  If the SERVICE CONNECTED PERCENTAGE prompt (field .302) entered"
16578:^DD(2,".361",21,10,0)="        is 50% or greater 'SERVICE CONNECTED 50% TO 100%' can be"
16579:^DD(2,".361",21,11,0)="        selected."
16580:^DD(2,".361",21,12,0)="   "
16581:^DD(2,".361",21,13,0)="    b.  Otherwise, the percentage is assumed to be less than 50% and"
16582:^DD(2,".361",21,14,0)="        only 'SC, LESS THAN 50%' may be entered."
16583:^DD(2,".361",21,15,0)="   "
16584:^DD(2,".361",21,16,0)="2.  If the response to the WERE YOU A PRISONER OF WAR field (# .525)"
16585:^DD(2,".361",21,17,0)="    is YES and the veteran is not service connected, you must select "
16586:^DD(2,".361",21,18,0)="    PRISONER OF WAR as the eligibility code."
16587:^DD(2,".361",21,19,0)="   "
16588:^DD(2,".361",21,20,0)="3.  If the response to the CURRENT PH INDICATOR field (#.531) "
16589:^DD(2,".361",21,21,0)="    is YES and the veteran is not service connected and is not a Prisoner"
16590:^DD(2,".361",21,22,0)="    of War, you must select PURPLE HEART RECIPIENT as the eligibility code."
16591:^DD(2,".361",21,23,0)=" "
16592:^DD(2,".361",21,24,0)="4.  If the veteran is receiving VA benefits, but does not meet the"
16593:^DD(2,".361",21,25,0)="    criteria in items 1 and 2 above, then the following choices may"
16594:^DD(2,".361",21,26,0)="    be presented for selection:"
16595:^DD(2,".361",21,27,0)=" "
16596:^DD(2,".361",21,28,0)="    If RECEIVING A&A BENEFITS is answered YES, the eligibility code"
16597:^DD(2,".361",21,29,0)="    AID & ATTENDANCE may be selected."
16598:^DD(2,".361",21,30,0)=" "
16599:^DD(2,".361",21,31,0)="    If the RECEIVING HOUSEBOUND BENEFITS is answered YES ,the eligibility"
16600:^DD(2,".361",21,32,0)="    code HOUSEBOUND may be selected."
16601:^DD(2,".361",21,33,0)=" "
16602:^DD(2,".361",21,34,0)="    If the above two prompts were answered NO, but the RECEIVING A VA"
16603:^DD(2,".361",21,35,0)="    PENSION prompt was answered YES, only the NSC, VA PENSION prompt"
16604:^DD(2,".361",21,36,0)="    may be selected."
16605:^DD(2,".361",21,37,0)=" "
16606:^DD(2,".361",21,38,0)="5.  If none of the above pertain to this veteran, then the NSC eligibility"
16607:^DD(2,".361",21,39,0)="    will be available for selection."
16608:^DD(2,".361",21,40,0)=" "
16609:^DD(2,".361",21,41,0)="**  Dependent on the birthdate of the applicant, the following two"
16610:^DD(2,".361",21,42,0)="    eligibility codes may be displayed along with those shown in items"
16611:^DD(2,".361",21,43,0)="    3 through 5 above:  WORLD WAR I and MEXICAN BORDER WAR.  These would"
16612:^DD(2,".361",21,44,0)="    display for veterans not meeting the criteria in items 1 and 2, but"
16613:^DD(2,".361",21,45,0)="    whose date of birth is prior to 1907."
16614:^DD(2,".361","AUDIT")="y"
