23446:^DD("2.312","8.03",0)="EB DISPLAY ENTRY^P365'^IBCN(365,^8;3^Q"
23447:^DD("2.312","8.03",3)="Enter a valid IIV Response entry."
23448:^DD("2.312","8.03",21,0)="^^3^3^3160128^"
23449:^DD("2.312","8.03",21,1,0)="This field will contains a pointer to the IIV Response entry that was "
23450:^DD("2.312","8.03",21,2,0)="manually or automatically accepted.  It is used to display fields from "
23451:^DD("2.312","8.03",21,3,0)="the IIV Response file in the Eligibility Benefits action."
23452:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,0)="^^6^6^3160128^"
23453:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,1,0)="Before this field is set, it is checked to see if it contains a previous "
23454:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,2,0)="value.  If it does, the DO NOT PURGE field (#.11) in the IIV Response "
23455:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,3,0)="file (#365) of the previously set entry is set to 0. This allows the  "
23456:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,4,0)="previous IIV Response entry to be purged the next time the purge is run."
23457:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,5,0)="The DO NOT PURGE flag of the current IIV Response entry is then set to 1"
23458:^DD("2.312","8.03",23,6,0)="to prevent it from being purged."
